{"title":"Take Me Home, Country Roads","description":"The full song, with one robotic singer over the original instrumental music. Follow each syllable and the sung pitch in the scrolling score.","bpm":82,"duration":195.8504375,"presentation":"solo-roll","parts":[{"id":"lead","kind":"voice","name":"Country Roads","role":"One voice","body":{"female":0,"child":0},"volume":0.602432,"pan":0,"vibrato":22,"telemetryEncoding":"gzip","voice":{"breathiness":0.045,"brightness":0.65,"tension":0.55},"melody":{"name":"Take Me Home, Country Roads","source":"CMUdict syllables and timed CHIMERA mouth gestures, aligned to the supplied complete John Denver recording. Vocal pitch, word timing and vowel holds are estimated from that recording.","lyrics":"Almost heaven, West Virginia, Blue Ridge Mountains, Shenandoah River. Life is old there, older than the trees, younger than the mountains, growing like a breeze. Country Roads, take me home, to the place, I belong, West Virginia, Mountain Mama. Take me home, Country Roads, All my memories gather round her, Miner's lady, stranger to blue water Dark and dusty, painted on the sky, misty taste of moonshine, teardrop in my eye. Country Roads, take me home to the place I belong, West Virginia Mountain Mama. Take me home, Country Roads. I hear her voice in the morning hour as she calls me. The radio reminds me of my home far away. Driving down the road I get a feeling that I should have been home yesterday yesterday Country Roads, take me home to the place I belong. West Virginia Mountain Mama take me home Country Roads Country Roads, Take me home to the place I belong, West Virginia Mountain Mama take me home Country Roads me home. Country Roads, take me home. Country Roads.","duration":195.8504375,"notes":[{"start":6.45,"duration":0.225,"midi":63.0,"lyricIndex":0},{"start":6.68,"duration":0.195,"midi":63.0,"lyricIndex":0,"hold":true},{"start":6.88,"duration":0.185,"midi":63.0,"lyricIndex":0,"hold":true},{"start":7.07,"duration":0.775,"midi"